maria: quick a11y check — when I open the Insights side panel with the keyboard the tab order stops after the search input. focus doesn't land on the Close (X) or the first card. possible keyboard trap? can someone repro? :thinking:
dan: i can repro on mac + voiceover. panel has role=dialog but we don't move focus into the panel on open. also background is still tabbable (annoying).
kelsey: thanks — that matches what i saw. proposal: on open run focusManager.focus(panel.querySelector('[data-focus-first]')) and set aria-hidden=true on the main app container until panel closes. also we should expose a visible focus indicator in dark theme (current 1px outline is nearly invisible).
samir: agree. small snippet for the open handler (pseudo):
```js
// on panel open
panel.setAttribute('role', 'dialog');
panel.setAttribute('aria-modal', 'true');
const first = panel.querySelector('[data-focus-first]') || panel.querySelector('button, a, input');
if (first) first.focus();
mainApp.setAttribute('aria-hidden', 'true');
// on close: remove aria-hidden, restore focus to triggering control
```
keeps it simple and avoids tabbing into background.
a11y-bot: Lighthouse contrast check: panel primary CTA color #0070f3 on white bg = 3.9:1 (fails 4.5). small change needed for text/button contrast.
maria: good catch. can we tweak CTA to #005bb5 or add a 1px darker border to bump ratio? also let's ensure focus ring color meets contrast on both light & dark themes.
dan: quick cross-browser note — Narrator will announce the dialog if focus is properly moved, but if aria-hidden is still not set on background you get spurious announcements from page content. test matrix: VoiceOver, NVDA, Narrator.
kelsey: i'll prototype with aria-hidden toggling + stronger focus ring and post screenshots. also adding data-focus-first attr to the panel header close button so keyboard users can escape immediately.
maria: sounds good. can you throw the branch into a small PR and tag me? i'll run the accessibility smoke tests afterwards. :thumbsup:
